 known why a  select few are allowed to enter while  the vast majority are not the strike  palace was named as such due to its  similar appearance to the Shrike  creature the structure was domed with  many jagged arches and buttresses giving  it a bladed and thorned look eventually  it is revealed that the strikes tree of  pain was in fact not a physical tree at  all but an advanced simulation within  the shrikes palace lay countless humans  connected by neural interface within the  simulation they experienced  incomprehensible amounts of pain pain  which the Shrike broadcasted into the  void which binds attempting to draw out  the enemy of the AI ultimate  intelligence the human ultimate  intelligence like the crystal monolith  almost nothing is known of the nature or  purpose of the cave tombs just that they  are a group of caves which exist in the  valley of the time tombs the Jade tomb  however stands out due to the green glow  it emits the entrance to the labyrinth  of Hyperion also waited at the base of  the jade tombs Hyperion was one of the  nine labyrinthine worlds which each  contained a mysterious system of  underground tunnels the labyrinths were  created by some long-gone race which the  humans of the hegemony named the  builders the actual purpose of the Jade  tombs may in some way be related to some  exotic Auster's who have been bred to  survive on gaseous planets  the purpose of the obelisk tomb remains  ambiguous though it is vaguely suggested  that it could contain the Shrike army  glimpsed by the character fed monk Assad  at some point in the future this is not  clear however the obelisk could also in  some way be related to the Brotherhood  of mieux a seemingly religious group  interested in shaping mankind's destiny  who vanished from galactic society after  the hegemony fell Dan Simmons leaves  much of the detail concerning the  purpose and the origin of the time tombs  open though it seems to be clear that  they are tied directly into the purpose  of the Shrike  [Music]
 

